  "context_markdown": "This public register records known, intentional differences between the supplied printed source and the present working edition. Entries are ordered by movement and local bar. These choices are adopted for this edition; their inclusion does not establish the original transcribers' intentions.\n\nThe review covers all four movements and all 18 pages of the supplied scan, compared with a 19-page native MuseScore rendering, with magnified checks of identified passages. It is a source comparison, not an independent note-by-note retranscription, a collation of all surviving sources or a guarantee that every small mark has been independently verified. The printed source is the Breitkopf & Härtel collected edition (1862), reprinted by Dover (1970), not an autograph.\n\nBar numbers restart in each movement. The slow movement and Scherzo have opening pickups; split repeat bars are not counted as additional numbered bars. Locations follow the displayed native score numbering. Excerpts show the specified location with neighbouring context; clef entries show a representative opening, not necessarily the complete passage.",
